finding: P1: src/core/rendering/tonemapping.ts:39-42 and src/core/rendering/upscaling.ts:35-38 interpret every upper scene's alpha as premultiplied coverage, but standard opaque surfaces do not produce that invariant: src/standard/rendering/pipelines.ts:85 passes through material alpha, including AlphaMode.Opaque. Independently reproduced with a standard unlit opaque red cube (baseColor [1,0,0,0.2]) in the upper camera, antialias off, Tonemapping.None, over a lower clear-only camera: its fully covered center is [102,0,204,255] over blue, then [102,204,0,255] when only the lower clear becomes green, instead of opaque red. Thus lower presentation leaks into higher opaque pixels and the new core points test passes without exercising it. Preserve opaque alpha semantics at the renderer boundary and add a regression that actually covers this shipped path.
